    "type": "question",
    "label": "42",
    "prompt": "Solve the following equation.\n$$9^x-26(3^x)-27=0.$$",
    "layout": "list",
    "columns": null,
    "questionDiagrams": [],
    "children": [],
    "answer": {
      "short": "$x=3$.",
      "worked": "Let $u=3^x>0$, so $9^x=u^2$.\n$$\\begin{align*}u^2-26u-27&=0\\\\(u-27)(u+1)&=0\\\\u&=27\\text{ or }u=-1.\\end{align*}$$\nReject $u=-1$ because $3^x>0$.\n$$\\begin{align*}3^x&=27\\\\3^x&=3^3\\\\x&=3.\\end{align*}$$",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
    },
    "answerSpaceMm": 35
  },
